<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">O'Brien dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Uí Briain, Ua Briain</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The O'Brien dynasty, in Irish Uí Briain, was a royal family of Munster descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru">Brian Boru</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-cais">Dál gCais</a>. From the 11th century they ruled as kings of Munster and later of Thomond, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limerick">Limerick</a> as their chief seat, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muirchertach-ua-briain">Muirchertach Ua Briain</a> claimed the high kingship of Ireland. In 1543 Murrough O'Brien submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a> and became Earl of Thomond.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/obrien-dynasty.jpg" alt="O'Brien dynasty" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Sodacan /; derivative work by Retroplum · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:O%27Brien_Arms.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
